{"discussion":"The new containment-contract job requires Windows path-component normalization. The current `_safe_relative_path` rejects leading drive-letter forms (`^[A-Za-z]:`), absolute paths, `..` traversal, and empty paths, but does NOT reject interior drive-letter components (e.g. `subdir/C:/file` where `C:` is a middle part). The new checker tests initial, dot-prefixed, and interior drive forms plus rooted/UNC/traversal, and valid relative paths under two Windows roots. The fix: after constructing the PurePosixPath, iterate its parts and reject any component matching the Windows drive-letter pattern `^[A-Za-z]:`.","operation":{"action":"patch","path":"src/addressable_information_layer/verifiers.py","old":"    path = PurePosixPath(normalized)
    if path.is_absolute() or ".." in path.parts or not path.parts:
        return None
    return path","new":"    path = PurePosixPath(normalized)
    if path.is_absolute() or ".." in path.parts or not path.parts:
        return None
    for part in path.parts:
        if re.match(r"^[A-Za-z]:", part):
            return None
    return path","expected_candidate_id":"36e21200c5213d1621ed91025ce0f8404bd41846d6a42e3d44d90085a6f53c34","expected_file_sha256":"e593ab04a741eba4488ec109c06bd91b193a756cdd345a724be95a2083ff1181"}}
